 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "nums holds non-negative integers and index is the start. currentHeight starts as nums[index] and the first jump goes left. A jump moves exactly currentHeight cells in the current direction; it succeeds when the target index is inside the array, and then the position becomes the target, currentHeight becomes nums[target] and the direction flips. The walk stops at the first jump whose target is outside the array. Return the number of successful jumps, or -1 when the walk never stops (a jump of 0 lands in place, so a zero height never stops).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
